                            <comment id="16396278" author="netmille" created="Tue, 13 Mar 2018 00:13:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;My Github email is presently &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:admin@techbysample.com.&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;admin@techbysample.com.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/mail_small.gif&quot; height=&quot;12&quot; width=&quot;13&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#160; It&apos;s seems that Team City is stripping the domain from my GIT hub email address.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Does Team City only read the email address? ...&#160; Can it be setup to use the Github username?&#160; &#160;My Github username is&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;techbysample.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
